# Netlify Basic Auth — page-specific access control.
# Add blocks below to protect a page/folder with the browser's native
# username+password prompt. Delete a block (or the whole file) to make
# that path public again — no redeploy config changes needed beyond
# pushing the updated file.
#
# Example:
# /pages/some-page.html
#   Basic-Auth: username:password
#
# (Connection Reuse is currently gated a different way — see
# pages/connection-reuse-gate.html — a custom on-brand passcode page,
# not Basic Auth. No rule needed here for it.)
